    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0292" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.9318/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 21.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chinese Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 4th instant, in which you are good enough to inform
                    me that appropriate instructions have been sent by telegraph to the American
                    Minister at San Jose for the diplomatic and consular representatives to use
                    their good offices, with the consent of the Costa Rican Government, in behalf of
                    the Chinese residents in that country in case of need.</p>
                <p>I beg to express to you the sincere thanks of my Government for your kind
                    compliance with its request.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kai Fu Shah</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
